WEBVTT

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:12.110
Please enjoy your stay.

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:17.550
Welcome to "Heaven" songolmaria, please enjoy your visit.

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:21.530
Whoa!!! Look, look Nii-chan!

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:25.420
We're so high and the view is great!
Don't you think so?!

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:28.010
From up here, people look like roadside trash!

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:31.020
Isami... saying it that way is very cruel...

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:34.590
Uhmm... You seem very tense there Nii-chan!

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:36.590
You promised we could take it easy today...

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:38.600
Yeah, you're right.

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:43.600
Although, after you finished with classes, I didn't expect you to do that.

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:47.040
I challenge you to a cooking duel! I'll show you!

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:50.770
Wait for what is to come, Yukihira Soma!

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:54.960
We meet again!

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:56.490
Shut up! Don't talk me!

00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:04.700
Miss...

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:06.990
...you sure about this?

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:10.990
Please see yourself to the elevator!

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:16.340
In Japan there is saying that goes: "You can make a fresh start if you walk up to a high place."

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:19.940
Oh, really...

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:24.720
Even though you are on top,

00:01:25.610 --> 00:01:28.260
Juts you wait, Yukihira!

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:31.210
Are you thinking about Yukihira again?

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:38.620
What are you doing?

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:44.970
Stop jumping Isami!!

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:49.870
I told you to stop Isami!!!!

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:27.520
Jeez... You're still angry Nii-chan?

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:28.920
Of course!

00:03:28.970 --> 00:03:33.550
I almost died! I mean you're an inconvenience to all those around!

00:03:33.670 --> 00:03:38.280
Sorry, sorry. But you dwell on a lot of different things all the time, Nii-chan.

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:39.850
Well...

00:03:39.850 --> 00:03:41.170
I'm sorry for worrying you...

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:45.720
Guys, the planetarium is over here!

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:48.110
Today, all my fellow dorm members and I are together!

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:49.730
Now this is how to spend one's youth!

00:03:49.810 --> 00:03:51.030
This is how to enjoy school life!

00:03:51.090 --> 00:03:52.900
This is how we affirm our brotherly bonds!

00:03:53.450 --> 00:03:56.190
You call this enjoying school life?

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:58.170
You're right.

00:03:58.230 --> 00:04:03.060
I wanted to go see the postcard collection of Japan, which is housed in this museum!

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:05.380
That's not what I meant...

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:10.560
In the next place we go, we have to have lots of fun-

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:11.220
Right Nii-chan?

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:13.090
Yes, of course.

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:15.480
But, where can we go?

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:18.040
Well... about that...

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:31.700
I entreat you to press onward, Lady Erina.

00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:36.640
We must assemble on the thirtieth floor

00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:36.640
and evaluate the merit of a French dish.

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:38.610
Henceforth from then, your scheduled

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:38.610
affairs for the today will concluded.

00:04:38.610 --> 00:04:40.750
So only three on the schedule today?

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:46.860
Pardon my ignorance, but is something amiss Lady Erina?

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:48.960
I-I-Izaku...

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:50.970
It would be nice to spend just a moment

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:50.970
attending to another matter as well...

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:52.560
It would. whatever could such a matter be?

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:53.690
F-For..the...

00:04:54.070 --> 00:04:55.160
Penguins!

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:56.370
The Penguins!?

00:04:56.380 --> 00:04:58.970
As expected of Lady Erina!

00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:02.410
In little more than a moment, my feeble and

00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:02.410
humble mind can conjure exactly how you

00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:02.410
will "attend" to the matter of the Penguins!

00:05:02.410 --> 00:05:03.540
You're wrong!!!!

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:07.140
T-Then, what in your infinite wisdom and benevolence,

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:07.140
could you be planning to do with penguins ?

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:10.330
Do not let it be so that your ladyship intends

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:10.330
to cook the innocent penguins...! ( ; o , )!

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:11.880
I-I would never even think about doing something that cruel!!!

00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:13.640
Just forget it!

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:15.600
Really? In that event, Lady Erina, then...

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:19.460
Welcome to our establishment!

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:22.140
Isami... What is <i>this... place!?</i>

00:05:22.140 --> 00:05:24.570
While taking it easy together, I also wanted to visit this place.

00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:26.290
This cosplay-cafe.

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:28.590
A cos...play...cafe...?

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:32.740
As I have received your order, I

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:32.740
shall now inform the kitchen staff.

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:37.310
I-lsami...you wanted to visit someplace like this...?

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:40.320
I really like the Japanese culture...

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:42.130
the traditions,

00:05:42.340 --> 00:05:43.630
the costumes,

00:05:43.640 --> 00:05:45.600
and their holidays and festivals.

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:47.610
<i>Everything</i> seems here matches my "interests".

00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:52.350
You only have to look around to realize this place is unique,

00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:55.200
even if there are some places similar to it.

00:05:55.610 --> 00:05:59.260
Customers are also allowed to cosplay.

00:05:59.260 --> 00:06:01.860
They even lend clothing in places like this.

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:04.700
A cosplay they lend to customers...

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:07.640
NEVER FEAR! The Cabbage and Orange Twins are here!!

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:09.780
OH DEAR GOD NOOOOOOOOOO!!!!!!!

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:10.950
Oh Master.

00:06:11.790 --> 00:06:13.800
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:18.490
With my arcane arts. I infuse this dish with the essence of...

00:06:18.490 --> 00:06:20.500
cabbage flavor!!!

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:29.300
S-So... here we have both of your omelets,

00:06:29.720 --> 00:06:33.250
made with all of my love!

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:36.010
U-uh...ah...thank you very much.

00:06:36.010 --> 00:06:38.140
Wait a second...

00:06:38.140 --> 00:06:40.150
I've seen that girl before...

00:06:40.150 --> 00:06:44.050
Oh: don't kid.~ That's just your way

00:06:40.150 --> 00:06:44.050
of flirting with me to imply I'm cute!

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:46.020
Well...l don't...

00:06:48.030 --> 00:06:53.180
Now lets add a magical spell that

00:06:48.030 --> 00:06:53.180
omelet taste better! On my mark !

00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:06.460
Hence. thou tasty omelet, becomes even

00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:06.460
tastier with our combined might!!

00:07:07.140 --> 00:07:09.690
...becomes even tastier with our combined might!!

00:07:12.250 --> 00:07:14.300
Please enjoy your meal!

00:07:18.530 --> 00:07:19.290
F***!!

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:22.220
My table just had to be people from my school!!

00:07:22.220 --> 00:07:25.190
Now everyone at school will find

00:07:22.220 --> 00:07:25.190
out I work in a shi**ole Iike this!!!!

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:29.510
Ufara-chan, we have another omelet order for table 10.

00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:31.480
I'll be right there!!

00:07:31.980 --> 00:07:33.610
THANK YOU VERY MUCH FOR YOUR PATRONAGE!

00:07:34.700 --> 00:07:38.220
That was a <i>fun</i> place. Don't you think, Nii-chan?

00:07:38.220 --> 00:07:39.520
"Become even tastier!"

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:40.780
Shut up, lsamu!!!

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:43.880
Your teasing aside,

00:07:43.880 --> 00:07:47.060
that omelet was very delicious. TOO DELICIOUS...

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:48.990
Are you, gonna punch it since its 'suspicious'?

00:07:49.070 --> 00:07:53.930
The egg was <i>just right </i>and the rice was

00:07:49.070 --> 00:07:53.930
prepared <i>so</i> nicely. Its too 'suspicious'.

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:56.660
You don't think it was just the magic spell "we" cast?

00:07:56.660 --> 00:07:59.930
lts either something that simple

00:07:56.660 --> 00:07:59.930
or the work of an enemy stand...

00:07:59.930 --> 00:08:01.520
Nii-chan...did you hit your head,

00:07:59.930 --> 00:08:01.520
you seem grumpier than normal?

00:08:03.110 --> 00:08:04.990
Hey, Hayama-kun! Here it is!!

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:11.740
I asked them to add your name as you are also going

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:11.740
to help choose the species too, Hayama-kun!

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:15.930
Putting down just your name "Jun" should've been more than enough.

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:19.620
Don't call me "Jun", call me "Shiomi"!

00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:23.970
Even so... A person with my name isn't going to be preparing a dish with it.

00:08:24.350 --> 00:08:26.110
'How come'?

00:08:27.960 --> 00:08:29.500
Oh well, I guess.

00:08:31.290 --> 00:08:34.780
Its been a long time since we've come here. Wouldn't you say?

00:08:34.810 --> 00:08:38.750
Yeah, even if we're cooks, we should still make time to stop by occasionally.

00:08:41.100 --> 00:08:43.960
If I had to prepare pork-topped rice, I would use this dish,

00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:47.430
but I would use this one to follow the other recipe...

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:52.420
Let's use this, let's use this for cooking from now on, Nikumi!

00:08:52.710 --> 00:08:54.850
Never, ever call me Meatumi again or so help me!

00:08:54.850 --> 00:08:57.370
I'll castrate you and serve the scraps to you for dinner!!!

00:08:58.810 --> 00:09:00.470
Look, look Nii-chan!

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:03.170
This pizza display looks like the real deal!

00:09:03.400 --> 00:09:05.910
Damn this looks soooo real and good too!

00:09:06.290 --> 00:09:07.800
I'd love to try this Italian pasta twister thing!

00:09:08.010 --> 00:09:10.230
How could simple dishes be made so appealing, huh...

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:16.680
Please Takumi sir, try my humble dish!

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:16.680
Afterwards I'd like to make you a margarita!

00:09:16.680 --> 00:09:18.650
No, please try my lasagna sir!

00:09:18.650 --> 00:09:21.750
No, better yet try my pasta!

00:09:21.750 --> 00:09:23.800
Okay. if you want my opinion, Japanese

00:09:21.750 --> 00:09:23.800
chefs making dishes from my homeland,

00:09:23.800 --> 00:09:27.530
I'd be happy to give you my impressions.

00:09:27.530 --> 00:09:29.000
Nah, better not...

00:09:29.800 --> 00:09:33.820
Please, show me how to cook your dishes!

00:09:33.820 --> 00:09:35.830
Give me a chance too!

00:09:35.830 --> 00:09:37.420
I want a be a pupil as well!

00:09:37.420 --> 00:09:38.170
WHAT IN THE WORLD!?

00:09:41.320 --> 00:09:43.240
FU##EN YUKIHIRAIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIII

00:09:43.240 --> 00:09:44.630
LET'S SEE WHOSE DISH REALLY TASTES BETTER,

00:09:44.630 --> 00:09:46.640
AND PROVE WHO DESERVES TO BE ADORED

00:09:44.630 --> 00:09:46.640
BY DISCIPLES LIKE IN MY DREAMS!!!!

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:48.610
AND WE'LL DO IT IN A

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:48.610
DUEEEELLLLLL!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!

00:09:48.610 --> 00:09:50.910
Nii-chan really likes to think about Yukihira,

00:09:50.910 --> 00:09:52.500
guess I better start calling Yukihira "Nii-chan" as well...

00:09:54.310 --> 00:09:57.950
That's the same look Yuki always has on his face,

00:09:57.950 --> 00:10:00.040
he's definitely always looked like that.

00:10:00.050 --> 00:10:02.770
Well, to tell you the truth, l had my doubts coming along.

00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:06.370
Yuki-chan, you're very cautious.

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:19.230
Then Megumi was all like "l've never

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:19.230
eaten any thing like this before.",

00:10:19.400 --> 00:10:21.450
So, we didn't get any and left.

00:10:21.450 --> 00:10:26.360
And that is how we then wound up

00:10:21.450 --> 00:10:26.360
running into Takumichi and Isamichi.

00:10:26.360 --> 00:10:27.650
Takumichi...?

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:28.870
Isamichi...?

00:10:29.620 --> 00:10:33.480
Sorry you were both called <i>that</i> so

00:10:29.620 --> 00:10:33.480
confidently, I'm sure she's sorry too.

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:37.460
There's no need to apologize. in Italy, its

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:37.460
normal for people to go by given names.

00:10:38.590 --> 00:10:40.220
Fuhgeddaboudit!

00:10:40.220 --> 00:10:41.560
What would you lot be ordering today?

00:10:43.070 --> 00:10:45.500
For now, let's start with something light.

00:10:45.500 --> 00:10:48.900
Megumi, since it's your first time

00:10:45.500 --> 00:10:48.900
here, order whatever you want

00:10:49.530 --> 00:10:50.910
Whaaaaa-me? Ummmmm--

00:10:51.660 --> 00:10:55.850
then how about the lean gugokumonju and pork fried rice?

00:10:57.190 --> 00:10:58.570
We can also add cheese!

00:10:58.580 --> 00:11:01.050
I love cheese on anything!

00:11:01.050 --> 00:11:03.560
You're right, that does sound good

00:11:04.900 --> 00:11:06.160
Well then, make it two of those!

00:11:06.160 --> 00:11:07.620
Them youngsters don't understand a single thing. No siree!

00:11:09.010 --> 00:11:11.650
No one should be putting fried rice and <i>cheese</i> together.

00:11:11.650 --> 00:11:15.580
Tis just needs a sprinklin' of seasonin' with 'some

00:11:11.650 --> 00:11:15.580
cabbage and seaweed for garnish... Kids these days.

00:11:15.590 --> 00:11:19.770
If its the first time ye be trying that

00:11:15.590 --> 00:11:19.770
dish, eat it the proper Japanese way.

00:11:22.460 --> 00:11:23.500
S-Sorry!

00:11:24.760 --> 00:11:25.720
Tadokoro-san,

00:11:25.720 --> 00:11:28.200
there was no need to apologize.

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:35.150
We decided to order what we wanted,
I don't recall asking the opinion of some stranger.

00:11:35.150 --> 00:11:36.620
What 'd you just say, you lil shit?!?!

00:11:37.160 --> 00:11:39.170
C-calm down Bun-san.

00:11:39.170 --> 00:11:41.140
Sorry, normally he is very cheerful and kind,

00:11:41.140 --> 00:11:44.070
But lately he has been in a bad mood.

00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:50.400
Anyway, a group of children hasn't the first clue in their

00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:50.400
noggins 'bout the ingredients needed fer a dish that traditional.

00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:55.850
Now if you're done spouting your <i>"wisdom"</i>, senile old fool.

00:11:57.990 --> 00:12:01.590
I'll have you know we are <i><u>chefs</u></i> and

00:12:01.590 --> 00:12:03.600
I will <i><u>NOT</u></i> keep quiet if someone insults

00:12:01.590 --> 00:12:03.600
our skill and knowledge at our own trade.

00:12:03.890 --> 00:12:05.690
Oh fancy yerself chefs do you...?

00:12:05.690 --> 00:12:08.670
Its true we are not as acquainted with Japanese cuisine,

00:12:09.510 --> 00:12:12.150
But we both respect and appreciate Japanese cuisine,

00:12:12.610 --> 00:12:16.340
Yet saying we're fools who don't know how to use our heads to 'harness our talents and creativity toward cuisine, is an insult !!

00:12:16.340 --> 00:12:20.820
That's right, we like the culture and

00:12:16.340 --> 00:12:20.820
cuisine of Japan a great deal.

00:12:20.990 --> 00:12:22.960
I understand now, you're all ignorant--

00:12:23.380 --> 00:12:25.180
FOREIGNERS!

00:12:25.810 --> 00:12:30.200
We understand <i>perfectly</i> what Japanese cuisine and

00:12:25.810 --> 00:12:30.200
culture is without someone like you <i>preaching</i> about it.

00:12:31.920 --> 00:12:32.970
Interesting.

00:12:32.970 --> 00:12:35.780
Face me in a duel, <i>boy</i>.

00:12:35.780 --> 00:12:38.120
Whoev'r makes the most scrumptious dish,

00:12:40.130 --> 00:12:44.070
will be the 'pro' and so the other <i>kitch'n</i>

00:12:40.130 --> 00:12:44.070
should understand the 'pro' is right.

00:12:44.070 --> 00:12:47.050
You just have to make a dish more delicious than me,

00:12:47.050 --> 00:12:47.590
<i>Goldielocks.</i>

00:12:47.590 --> 00:12:49.560
Sounds good to me,<i> geezer</i>.

00:12:49.560 --> 00:12:51.490
I accept your terms.

00:12:52.280 --> 00:12:53.460
Takumi-kun...

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:58.650
We have always represented and defended the

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:58.650
honor of Traporia Aldini from the hubris of outsiders.

00:12:59.530 --> 00:13:02.210
I <i>refuse</i> to stand idly back, while an ignorant <i>fool</i> insults us.

00:13:04.390 --> 00:13:06.650
Looks like Takumi is triggered now.

00:13:06.650 --> 00:13:08.670
In the name of the Aldini family,

00:13:10.130 --> 00:13:12.440
I will prepare the best dish this world has ever seen!!!

00:13:23.870 --> 00:13:27.270
The dishes we will cook shall be made with ingredients

00:13:23.870 --> 00:13:27.270
and cooking supplies from this very restaurant,

00:13:27.350 --> 00:13:29.320
That'll be the rules, by which the

00:13:27.350 --> 00:13:29.320
most delectable dish is decided.

00:13:31.330 --> 00:13:34.140
the owners and regulars of this restaurant shall be the judges.

00:13:34.140 --> 00:13:37.450
Just to be fair, Bun-san is someone I know,

00:13:37.450 --> 00:13:41.470
But I'm mainly here just to try new food,

00:13:37.450 --> 00:13:41.470
I promise to hold no personal bias.

00:13:41.640 --> 00:13:43.440
A man's palate can't lie!

00:13:44.070 --> 00:13:47.130
I understand, that works for me.

00:13:47.130 --> 00:13:49.810
But, I need to ask you something.

00:13:50.350 --> 00:13:51.110
What is it?

00:13:51.110 --> 00:13:54.460
We cook together as brothers.

00:13:54.460 --> 00:13:56.470
Can you <i>accept</i> that old man.

00:13:56.470 --> 00:14:01.410
I'll say this. one or two in the kitch'n doesn't matter

00:13:56.470 --> 00:14:01.410
<i>boy</i>, I don't need to <i>accept</i> something that trivial.

00:14:01.410 --> 00:14:03.420
Thank you, very much for your <i>understanding</i>.

00:14:03.840 --> 00:14:06.190
With all details settled.

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:08.830
I don't think you're qualified to be doing that...

00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:11.010
In this case,

00:14:12.060 --> 00:14:13.100
begin...

00:14:13.100 --> 00:14:14.020
the cooking!

00:14:16.920 --> 00:14:20.060
You'll soon learn to regret that attitude, once

00:14:16.920 --> 00:14:20.060
you lose this duel you irreverent child!

00:14:22.030 --> 00:14:23.790
So Japanese ingredients.

00:14:24.540 --> 00:14:27.430
And it appears that this isn't his first duel either.

00:14:27.600 --> 00:14:30.570
Bun-san isn't a professional,

00:14:30.570 --> 00:14:35.100
But in the last regional cooking

00:14:30.570 --> 00:14:35.100
competition I was in, he took first place.

00:14:36.360 --> 00:14:37.610
Kay, I'm about to go wild!

00:14:40.920 --> 00:14:41.890
Incredible!

00:14:41.890 --> 00:14:43.900
I can't believe he's that <i>good.</i>.

00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:45.660
High-stakes duels certainly bring out a chef's own "style".

00:14:46.620 --> 00:14:49.550
The experience and techniques accumulated

00:14:46.620 --> 00:14:49.550
in life brings out the best in a chef!

00:14:50.600 --> 00:14:52.610
While Ban was in top form in in this unplanned duel,

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:55.880
we are in bad shape

00:14:56.470 --> 00:15:01.830
now all that is left is to see if we can match his

00:14:56.470 --> 00:15:01.830
momentum and skill with these alien ingredients.

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:03.420
What should we do..?

00:15:04.300 --> 00:15:05.680
What can we do...?!

00:15:05.890 --> 00:15:07.150
If it was <i>him</i>

00:15:07.150 --> 00:15:11.090
I would have taken all the things I wanted at the start.

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:14.570
<i>That's</i> what I think about in a time like this!?

00:15:16.540 --> 00:15:20.180
Don't worry about him, that's just his "style"...

00:15:20.890 --> 00:15:22.860
Y-You're wrong! My inner voice isn't something to worry about!

00:15:23.110 --> 00:15:27.720
Heya Megumi. Does Takumi really think that's not weird?

00:15:27.720 --> 00:15:29.690
W-Well ...

00:15:29.690 --> 00:15:30.650
Of course!

00:15:30.660 --> 00:15:34.680
No matter the opponent, I just have

00:15:30.660 --> 00:15:34.680
to rely on what I always have.

00:15:35.770 --> 00:15:39.410
We just have to use our talent to make the best dish!

00:15:40.210 --> 00:15:41.380
You're right, Nii-chan.

00:15:41.380 --> 00:15:42.890
Well, almost there.

00:15:42.890 --> 00:15:46.160
To the bes' part of the, whole duel!!

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:48.840
Mmmmmm, this is...

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:52.940
It is an incredible aroma that defies description!

00:15:52.940 --> 00:15:56.340
Just the right amount of cabbage balances the

00:15:52.940 --> 00:15:56.340
scent and teases your appetite just enough!!

00:15:56.340 --> 00:15:59.020
And now, for the final touch,

00:15:59.560 --> 00:16:00.860
THIS!!

00:16:00.860 --> 00:16:02.580
S-Seaweed?!

00:16:02.580 --> 00:16:04.300
Is this allowed?

00:16:04.300 --> 00:16:06.850
Of course it's allowed!

00:16:07.230 --> 00:16:08.070
I see!

00:16:08.560 --> 00:16:12.210
Without that vital ingredient, my dish could not be a success.

00:16:14.310 --> 00:16:15.610
The aroma is so nice!

00:16:15.950 --> 00:16:19.050
This is the best type of sea weed,

00:16:19.470 --> 00:16:21.180
which gives an extra touch to the tantalizing scent.

00:16:21.690 --> 00:16:22.520
It's finished!

00:16:22.860 --> 00:16:24.530
It's my Cuman!

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:29.180
Ahhh. It brings back childhood memories...

00:16:29.190 --> 00:16:32.450
You're right, such nostalgia!

00:16:35.550 --> 00:16:36.730
Delicious!

00:16:37.100 --> 00:16:39.950
The mixture of the cabbage and spices is

00:16:37.100 --> 00:16:39.950
just perfect! It leaves a pleasant taste!

00:16:39.950 --> 00:16:41.960
It's like I'm floating, it feels so good!!

00:16:45.020 --> 00:16:46.700
Nii-chan... take this!

00:16:47.490 --> 00:16:49.000
Now you've done it!

00:16:50.390 --> 00:16:52.980
Although I expected something to

00:16:50.390 --> 00:16:52.980
knock my socks off, what he did...

00:16:52.980 --> 00:16:57.550
He crafted something simple to create a feeling of nostalgia.

00:16:58.720 --> 00:17:00.020
But we also have our own dish that can top that.

00:17:00.020 --> 00:17:02.030
Isami, let's start!

00:17:02.750 --> 00:17:03.750
Yes, Nii-chan!

00:17:06.980 --> 00:17:09.910
Don't you think you've used too much?

00:17:09.910 --> 00:17:10.750
Huh?

00:17:11.330 --> 00:17:13.430
Usually chefs don't use that much...

00:17:14.350 --> 00:17:15.610
Foolish youngsters, take'n Japan so lightly...

00:17:16.190 --> 00:17:18.460
Nah, this is all the effort we need to <i>win</i>.

00:17:20.970 --> 00:17:23.730
No matter what you try to cook, it ain't goin' to be any good.

00:17:24.150 --> 00:17:26.750
Maybe we are just foreigners here,

00:17:27.210 --> 00:17:31.530
But that means there are things

00:17:27.210 --> 00:17:31.530
that we are capable of you aren't.

00:17:32.450 --> 00:17:34.380
Stop yer respondin' and focus on yer cookin'!

00:17:34.460 --> 00:17:36.060
<i>TN: This is Japanese for "This motherfu##er..."</i>

00:17:38.360 --> 00:17:38.940
FORNO

00:17:39.240 --> 00:17:40.160
ARCHENTRECT.

00:17:41.080 --> 00:17:42.250
ISAMI! You're in charge of the cabbage!!

00:17:42.250 --> 00:17:43.510
I got you fam!

00:17:47.160 --> 00:17:47.660
Incredible!

00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:49.380
Such speed!

00:17:51.090 --> 00:17:51.930
So fierce ...!

00:17:53.190 --> 00:17:54.820
Hey? What happened with the...

00:17:54.820 --> 00:17:56.710
Fuhgeddaboudit!

00:17:57.210 --> 00:18:00.310
No matter what you may cook, you should

00:17:57.210 --> 00:18:00.310
always take the right amount of time!

00:18:02.110 --> 00:18:04.750
And that's because we use seeds to make-

00:18:06.510 --> 00:18:09.910
There are seeds in the rice!?!

00:18:10.530 --> 00:18:12.630
So its a Risotto?

00:18:12.880 --> 00:18:13.840
I see!

00:18:14.180 --> 00:18:17.450
I can't believe he had the time to mix everything perfectly!

00:18:18.030 --> 00:18:21.090
I thought you could only use what was in the restaurant...

00:18:21.470 --> 00:18:21.800
Wait that's-

00:18:23.150 --> 00:18:24.230
This seasoning is-

00:18:25.070 --> 00:18:26.410
And with this, we win!

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:28.300
This seaweed... it's different!

00:18:28.970 --> 00:18:30.020
This is isomori seaweed!

00:18:30.770 --> 00:18:34.370
Even in Italy, we use isomori seaweed,

00:18:35.090 --> 00:18:40.030
and we join both kinds of seaweed in harmony,

00:18:40.490 --> 00:18:41.620
fusing the flavor of Japan and Italy.

00:18:42.840 --> 00:18:44.510
Your dish is not just Italian cuisine!?

00:18:44.510 --> 00:18:46.730
If you aren't relying on just normal

00:18:44.510 --> 00:18:46.730
seaweed, I won't accept your dish!

00:18:57.790 --> 00:18:59.340
The texture as completely different!

00:18:59.760 --> 00:19:03.530
The cheese topping gives it wonderful flavor

00:18:59.760 --> 00:19:03.530
and harmony with the isomori! Amazing!

00:19:04.410 --> 00:19:07.010
As a dressing, we use a ketchup.

00:19:07.850 --> 00:19:10.740
As Italians, its natural for us to use tomatoes that way.

00:19:11.330 --> 00:19:13.970
This acidic flavor isn't just from the sauce.

00:19:14.600 --> 00:19:15.730
Clams?

00:19:16.690 --> 00:19:17.900
You guessed right, Tadokoro-san.

00:19:19.160 --> 00:19:21.840
Although this was not in the store to begin with,

00:19:22.770 --> 00:19:27.540
We used these clams even though they're rare in Italian food.

00:19:27.540 --> 00:19:34.330
If they're not used often in Italian

00:19:27.540 --> 00:19:34.330
cuisine, then why did you use them?

00:19:34.330 --> 00:19:38.730
That's... we wanted to incorporate

00:19:34.330 --> 00:19:38.730
Japanese elelments in our dish.

00:19:40.700 --> 00:19:42.960
Although Italy has come far in using foreign ingredients,

00:19:42.960 --> 00:19:49.490
it has not been easy for chefs to

00:19:42.960 --> 00:19:49.490
incorporate these foods into our cuisine,

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:51.510
and remains so to this day. But the

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:51.510
Japanese have a special form of canning,

00:19:51.510 --> 00:19:56.370
and thus they A can be eaten with nothing else.

00:19:57.670 --> 00:20:00.260
Things like that are why the Japanese are very good.

00:20:00.260 --> 00:20:03.110
Even if it's a dish is not made in Japan or by the Japanese.

00:20:04.750 --> 00:20:09.940
Japan is a nation that adopts any dish

00:20:04.750 --> 00:20:09.940
which further adds to its national richness

00:20:10.440 --> 00:20:14.880
As a result, although the menus in Japan may

00:20:10.440 --> 00:20:14.880
change overtime or certain dishes may evolve,

00:20:14.890 --> 00:20:19.410
but the Japanese never put aside

00:20:14.890 --> 00:20:19.410
the pride of their own recipes,

00:20:20.000 --> 00:20:21.460
Rather, the opposite is true.

00:20:22.890 --> 00:20:23.220
Am I mistaken?

00:20:24.140 --> 00:20:28.080
Those are the qualities I like about Japan.

00:20:29.090 --> 00:20:31.430
For example being in this place,

00:20:32.520 --> 00:20:33.610
we can all enjoy those dishes together.

00:20:35.920 --> 00:20:37.800
Do not think that with something like this

00:20:38.180 --> 00:20:40.150
I will recognize-

00:20:42.290 --> 00:20:46.010
My reluctance was overpowered by

00:20:42.290 --> 00:20:46.010
such an amazing first impression?!

00:20:46.690 --> 00:20:49.070
Something like this is possible...?

00:20:49.070 --> 00:20:52.590
This guy! He has released and captured

00:20:53.680 --> 00:20:55.650
the heart that I had so long closed off...

00:20:56.360 --> 00:20:58.160
I love Papa's fried rice a whole bunch?!

00:21:03.320 --> 00:21:05.240
What's wrong, Bun-San'?

00:21:05.250 --> 00:21:12.120
My daughter came the other day to

00:21:05.250 --> 00:21:12.120
tell me she was getting married...

00:21:12.830 --> 00:21:17.940
And to top it all off, he was blond foreigner just like that guy.

00:21:17.940 --> 00:21:22.300
And I said, "There is no way you're getting married!"

00:21:23.300 --> 00:21:25.860
Are you really so petty though?

00:21:25.860 --> 00:21:30.510
That's right! In spite of knowing it did not

00:21:25.860 --> 00:21:30.510
change anything, I could not help It.

00:21:30.510 --> 00:21:32.100
But...

00:21:32.100 --> 00:21:34.030
I understand now...

00:21:35.030 --> 00:21:37.800
When you encounter the culture of another country,

00:21:38.050 --> 00:21:40.520
You come to understand its good points

00:21:38.050 --> 00:21:40.520
as well as the things you dislike.

00:21:41.400 --> 00:21:45.380
Everything you've said is true.

00:21:48.440 --> 00:21:52.380
I'll tell my little girl tand hat dang

00:21:48.440 --> 00:21:52.380
foreigner fiance of hers as well.

00:21:52.970 --> 00:21:57.530
Alright, lets show how much we respect Japan one more time.

00:22:02.390 --> 00:22:04.150
Becomes even tastier with our combined might!

00:22:06.920 --> 00:22:07.380
Amazing!

00:22:07.380 --> 00:22:09.390
Now <i>that</i> is the culture of Japan!

00:22:19.990 --> 00:22:22.000
<i>FREE ITSDIOBRANDO!</i>

00:23:46.270 --> 00:23:48.370
In the end it was fun.

00:23:48.870 --> 00:23:53.010
Yeah, it was nice to see Takumi-kun and Isami-kun cook.

00:23:53.080 --> 00:23:58.410
Since the first time I saw you at school Takumi-kun, I've always though you were amazing. Don't you think so?

00:23:59.040 --> 00:24:00.160
You really think so...?

00:24:00.460 --> 00:24:01.460
But...

00:24:01.830 --> 00:24:07.850
But it was Yukihira's way of cooking without spending money which inspired me to do what I did...

00:24:08.020 --> 00:24:10.690
Perhaps today's victory was thanks to him?

00:24:10.830 --> 00:24:12.440
Ah, Soma-kun!

00:24:13.440 --> 00:24:16.460
Hey! Why is everyone in one big group?

00:24:16.490 --> 00:24:23.180
Listen to this, Yukihira...
Takumi was amazing!

00:24:26.240 --> 00:24:28.640
Wait a sec... that sounds delicious!

00:24:28.640 --> 00:24:32.090
Yo, Takumi!
Let me try your dish next time.

00:24:34.030 --> 00:24:39.370
That's right, I'm your rival so of course you want to taste it to find a way to best me in our next duel.

00:24:39.700 --> 00:24:41.650
Nawww, I wasn't even thinking about that when I asked.

00:24:42.680 --> 00:24:47.310
W-What are you saying!? Don't try to trick me into letting my guard down! I'll never fall for your tricks, Yukihira!

00:24:47.370 --> 00:24:48.370
Oh, Okay.

00:24:49.400 --> 00:24:51.000
Nii-chan, you tell him.
